@V := "tape" :: spec [active]
  version = "1.0"

@H 1172 := "METABOLISM / binding energy budget — does a real energy-in/out budget (starve -> die) self-regulate cell-count vs the external MAX_CELLS cap? (life-criterion MISSING #2: metabolism)" :: universe [🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE — a naive per-cell metabolism does NOT self-regulate count; population boom-busts to extinction (a_paper_negative_ok)]
  seed         = "Audit gap: the E ratchet in a_substrate_native_speak is a MOTIVATION scalar, not a binding metabolism. Real life consumes energy and dies when starved. H_1159b uses an EXTERNAL hard MAX_CELLS cap — a metabolic budget should replace it organically."
  substrate    = "toy $0 CPU. REUSE h1159b mitosis; ADD per-cell energy E: each step E -= upkeep; a cell GAINS E when it wins low-error assignments (it is 'useful'); division costs E; E<=0 -> cell dies. NO external cell cap."
  method       = "FROZEN FALSIFIER (pre-reg): 🟢 ENERGY-GATES iff the energy budget ALONE (no MAX_CELLS) regulates cell-count to track world complexity (Spearman(K_true,count)>=0.8) AND surviving cells are the low-error/useful ones (survival-usefulness corr>=0.5). 🔴 if energy can't self-regulate count or population collapses/explodes (a_paper_negative_ok)."
  verdict_tier = "🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE (toy numpy $0 CPU, 10 seeds, K_true ladder {3,5,8}, deterministic, p7, frozen pre-reg falsifier)"
  result       = "ALL FOUR conditions for 🟢 FAIL. F1 self-tuning: Spearman(K_true, final live count) = -0.699 << +0.8 — and NEGATIVE: higher world complexity dies MORE, the opposite of self-tuning. F2 survival-usefulness: Spearman(usefulness, survived) = +0.143 << +0.5 (directionally correct but far below bar; survivor mean reward 0.0103 > dead 0.0065). COLLAPSE guard FAIL: population goes EXTINCT in 25/30 runs (K=3 5/10 collapse, K=5 10/10, K=8 10/10; final count 0 in every K-mean). EXPLOSION guard pass (global peak only 5 cells, << 200 limit). MECHANISM (traced /tmp/diag3): population grows healthily (E accrues ~2.4, divides to 3-5 cells) then ALL cells starve SIMULTANEOUSLY in a ~50-step crash as later-onset clusters pull existing cells between competing centroids -> assignment error rises above the income threshold -> collective energy drain -> extinction; division COSTS energy precisely when energy is already draining, so mitosis cannot rescue the crash. FINDING: a naive per-cell metabolic budget is NOT a homeostatic capacity governor — it is a boom-bust predator-prey-like instability with NO negative-feedback floor; the external MAX_CELLS cap of H_1159b cannot be replaced by starvation alone. RULES OUT 'starvation = organic cell-count regulator' at toy scale; a stable metabolism would need an additional homeostatic term (e.g. density-dependent upkeep, an energy reservoir, or apoptosis-coupled birth control — cf 1171/1176)."
  construction = "ONE principled pre-scoring fix (a_completeness_over_cheap, H_1145-style defect guard): the initial D_REF=2.0 made the reward kernel give an ON-cluster oracle cell (assignment error ~1.65 = sigma*sqrt(DIM)) LESS income than upkeep -> EVERY cell starved trivially regardless of usefulness (collapse 30/30, an untestable regime, not a finding). Diagnosed via /tmp/diag*; rescaled D_REF=6.0 so on-cluster d~1.65 nets +0.019/step (a useful cell CAN survive) while between-cluster d~5 nets -0.003/step (a redundant cell starves) — making survival CONTINGENT on usefulness, the F1/F2 axis. After this fix the metabolism genuinely operates (cells divide, some survive at K=3) yet STILL collapses at K>=5 -> the collapse is a real dynamical result, not the defect. NO further tuning toward green (goalpost discipline, cf h1144/h1150)."
  scope        = "toy numpy $0 CPU prototype-split PROXY for CORE cell-division; toy energy model, NOT the live E ratchet; live engine + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope). p7."
  artifact     = "UNIVERSE/h1172_metabolism_energy_budget.py · .verdicts/1172_metabolism_energy_budget/H_1172.txt"
  xref         = "h1159b_mitosis_capacity_self_tuning · a_substrate_native_speak (E ratchet) · 1171_apoptosis_death · 1176_resource_competition · a_paper_negative_ok · p7 · a_scale_honest_scope"
